--TEST--
`Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep` still descends into a `secret` property but quotes neither side of the difference it finds there -- ADR 0092 § 5, ADR 0079 § 4
--FILE--
<?nvs
// ADR 0092 § 5's redaction row, at the one place this module renders a value a
// program declared `secret`. The two halves are separable and both are here:
// the comparison *descends* -- whether two secrets agree is not itself a
// secret, so a differing pair still fails and an agreeing pair still passes --
// while neither side is quoted back into a message a build log keeps.
//
// The redaction belongs to the property, not to the message: a non-secret
// sibling on the same class is quoted exactly as it would be on a class with
// no secret at all.

final class Cred {
    public function constructor(public string $user, public secret string $token) {}
}

final class Holder {
    public function constructor(public array<Cred> $creds) {}
}

int $refused = 0;

// The difference is found and reported -- at the property's own path, with
// both sides replaced. A member that skipped a secret property outright would
// print nothing here.
Cred $one = new Cred("ann", "s3cret-one");
Cred $two = new Cred("ann", "s3cret-two");
try { Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep($one, $two); } catch (Throwable $hidden) { $refused = $refused + 1; echo $hidden->message, "\n"; }

// The sibling, on the same class: quoted in full. The redaction is a property
// of the slot, not a mode the whole message enters.
Cred $bob = new Cred("bob", "same");
Cred $ann = new Cred("ann", "same");
try { Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep($bob, $ann); } catch (Throwable $shown) { $refused = $refused + 1; echo $shown->message, "\n"; }

// Composed through an array inside an object: the path still reads as a
// program would subscript it, and only the leaf is replaced.
Holder $left = new Holder([new Cred("ann", "one")]);
Holder $right = new Holder([new Cred("ann", "two")]);
try { Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep($left, $right); } catch (Throwable $under) { $refused = $refused + 1; echo $under->message, "\n"; }

// The other half of "still descends": two secrets that agree are an
// agreement, and the assertion passes rather than being skipped into either
// answer.
Cred $same = new Cred("ann", "same");
Cred $twin = new Cred("ann", "same");
Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep($same, $twin);
echo "agreed\n";

// Counted rather than read off the lines above: a member that started
// answering one of these instead of refusing fails here.
echo "refused=", $refused, "/3\n";
--EXPECT--
Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep failed: the two differ at `$actual->token`: `$actual` is «redacted», `$expected` is «redacted»
Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep failed: the two differ at `$actual->user`: `$actual` is "bob", `$expected` is "ann"
Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep failed: the two differ at `$actual->creds["0"]->token`: `$actual` is «redacted», `$expected` is «redacted»
agreed
refused=3/3
